# Best libraries for building Discord bots (by language and use case)

Pick the stack that makes you want to open the editor every day. Here’s a concise, practical map so you can choose fast and scale cleanly.

---

## Quick picks

- If you want the biggest ecosystem and plugins: discord.js (+ Sapphire) in TypeScript.
- If you want strict typing and modular design in Python: Hikari (+ Lightbulb or Tanjun).
- If you need serious performance and control: Rust (Twilight or Serenity).
- If you want rock-solid JVM tooling and voice: JDA (Java) or Kord (Kotlin).
- If you’re targeting low memory and simple deploys (e.g., Pi): DiscordGo (Go).

---

## Comparison by language

| Language | Library | Why choose it | Notable strengths | When to avoid |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| TypeScript/JS | discord.js | Largest community, docs, examples | Full interactions support, strong typings, ecosystem (Sapphire, discordx, builders, voice) | If you need ultra-low memory or non-Node runtime |
| TypeScript/JS | Oceanic.js (Eris successor) | High performance alt to d.js | Efficient sharding, lower overhead | Smaller ecosystem than d.js |
| TypeScript/JS (Deno) | Harmony | Deno-native dev flow | Type-safe, modern API | Smaller plugin ecosystem |
| Python | discord.py | Battle-tested classic | Mature docs, wide examples | Less “architected” than Hikari |
| Python | Hikari | Strict typing, modular core | Clean API, REST-only mode, flexible command frameworks (Lightbulb, Tanjun) | Slightly smaller community than d.py |
| Java | JDA | Enterprise-grade stability | Complete coverage, voice support, mature sharding | Heavier runtime footprint |
| Kotlin | Kord | Kotlin-first ergonomics | Coroutines, strong type-safety | Smaller than JDA |
| C#/.NET | Discord.Net | Established, reliable | Good docs, events model | Heavier than newer .NET libs |
| C#/.NET | Remora.Discord | Data-oriented, high-perf | Strong typing, concurrency focus | Smaller ecosystem |
| Go | DiscordGo | Lightweight, easy deploys | Low memory, simple binaries | Less ergonomic for complex state |
| Rust | Serenity | Ergonomic Rust wrapper | Good balance of features vs. complexity | Less modular than Twilight |
| Rust | Twilight | High-performance, modular | Fine-grained control, scalable shards | Steeper learning curve |
| C++ | DPP (D++) | Performance-focused | Scales to huge bots | Complex builds, steeper ramp |
| Elixir | Nostrum | BEAM-level concurrency | Fault-tolerance, hot upgrades | Niche ecosystem |
| PHP | DiscordPHP | PHP shop compatibility | Quick for existing PHP apps | Not ideal for high concurrency |
| Dart | nyxx | Flutter/Dart alignment | Cross-platform tooling | Smaller ecosystem |

